    <string name="tutorial_move_title">Move the window</string>
    <string name="tutorial_move_body">Apps open as windows on the screen. Hold the thin bar at the top of the window and drag it somewhere else.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_resize_title">Resize it</string>
    <string name="tutorial_resize_body">Hold the ◤ mark in the top-left corner and drag. The window grows or shrinks while the opposite corner stays put, and the app adapts to the new size.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_gesture_body">%1$s: %2$s\n\nNow try it on the sample window.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_fill_body">the window fills the screen and locks in place. Do the same gesture again to restore it.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_rotate_body">the app turns sideways and switches to its landscape layout. Do it again to turn it back upright.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_real_fullscreen_body">the app leaves the window and opens in real full screen. Handy for banking apps that do not work in a window. The apps button stays at the edge of the screen while you are in full screen.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_real_fullscreen_feedback">Would open in real full screen</string>
    <string name="tutorial_back_body">a Back press is sent to the app, just like the phone\'s own back gesture.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_back_feedback">← Back sent</string>
    <string name="tutorial_close_gesture_body">the window closes. The sample window will come back in a moment.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_close_title">Close the window</string>
    <string name="tutorial_close_body">The ✕ in the top-right corner closes the window. You can open as many windows of the same app as you like.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_apps_title">Apps button</string>
    <string name="tutorial_apps_body">This button gets you to your apps. Tap it to open the search, which also lists open apps. Hold it to close background apps. Drag it to move it.\n\nNow tap the highlighted button.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_desktops_title">Desktops</string>
    <string name="tutorial_desktops_body">You have more than one desktop. Swipe left or right in the highlighted bottom-left area to switch between them. Windows stay on their own desktop.\n\nNow swipe sideways in the highlighted area.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_settings_title">Settings</string>
    <string name="tutorial_settings_body">Hold an empty spot on the desktop for 1.5 seconds to open the settings. There you can change what gestures do, the window size and the screen refresh rate.\n\nNow hold an empty spot.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_done_title">You\'re all set!</string>
    <string name="tutorial_done_body">You can open this guide again any time from Settings → Show the guide again.</string>
